  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Rain-free conditions will persist through the \nend of October and possibly the first day of November\n\nCold front entering wrn NY and headed our way. It should pass\nthrough during the evening and early part of the night. Expect\nno precip from the clouds it generates, as there is only limited\nmoisture with it. The high pressure behind it is slightly milder\nthan the current airmass. Thus, temps and dewpoints should not\nbe as low for the next couple of days as the front stalls off to\nour south. It should return northward as a warm front Wed, but\nshould again only make clouds for Central PA. The next airmass\ndoes slide eastward instead of stalling overhead, and will help\nto set up a return, moist-er flow from the SW. But, it will take\na day or two to bring up enough moisture to build up enough to\nmake rain. It looks like Saturday night or Sunday would be the \nnext chc for precip.",
